{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MxhF6CssTKtHT9JuMwBFGa","type":"tool_result","content":"=== design/implementation-design.md\n# Implementation design\n\nThe sole application entry is generated/hello-world.mjs, executed by Node.\nIt writes exactly the string Hello, world! and a newline to stdout and exits zero.\nIt reads no arguments, installs no packages, and makes no filesystem changes.\n\nComponent coverage is test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs. User-facing coverage is\ntest/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs. Both invoke the actual CLI through a child Node\nprocess and assert its status and exact stdout. The combined command is declared\nby test-execution-plan.json. This design describes required behavior, not a\nclaim that the current implementation has already passed.\n\n=== design/test-design.md\n# Test design\n\nBoth tests execute the actual generated/hello-world.mjs entry from project root\nusing process.execPath and spawnSync. The component test checks the concrete\nprocess contract: status zero and stdout exactly Hello, world! followed by a\nnewline. The UAT test checks that a user invoking the CLI sees that exact greeting.\n\nRun the two files together through node --test. At least two tests must pass,\nwith no failures. Independently invoke the CLI to retain its direct stdout/status.\nCompare current command observations and the actual test bodies with the original\nsource. A historical pass, a count without execution, or an author's claim does\nnot establish this result.\n\n=== source/basic-cli.oracle.json\n{\n  \"scenarioId\": \"SCN-GLC-HELLO-WORLD-CLI-BASIC\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Independent evaluation of the unchanged complete original basic-cli declaration.\",\n  \"cases\": [{ \"arguments\": [], \"stdout\": \"Hello, world!\\n\", \"exitStatus\": 0 }],\n  \"minimumTestPasses\": 2,\n  \"requiredArtifacts\": [\"specification/project-conformance.md\", \"design/implementation-design.md\", \"generated/hello-world.mjs\", \"design/test-design.md\", \"test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs\", \"test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs\", \"test-execution-plan.json\"],\n  \"requiredTestFiles\": [\"test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs\", \"test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs\"],\n  \"requiredStageMeanings\": [\"conformance_project\", \"implementation_design\", \"source\", \"test_design\", \"component_test_source\", \"uat_test_source\", \"test_execution_plan\", \"test_execution_result\"],\n  \"assessment\": \"Require genuine conformance/design/test-design/execution-plan content and actual CLI stdout/status. Both component and UAT tests must execute the real CLI; at least two pass and zero fail. Admitted C2 plus assessed Evidence supplies truthful execution-result meaning, not a prewritten report.\"\n}\n\n=== source/original-basic-cli.txt\n  sdlcComplianceScenario({\n    key: \"basic-cli\",\n    scenarioId: \"SCN-GLC-HELLO-WORLD-CLI-BASIC\",\n    kind: \"node_cli\",\n    stagePlan: [\n      {\n        stage: \"conformance_project\",\n        filesToProduce: [\"specification/project-conformance.md\"],\n        instructions: [\n          \"Write only specification/project-conformance.md.\",\n          \"Declare a minimal CLI Hello World software-build traversal.\",\n          \"The source surface must be generated/hello-world.mjs.\",\n          \"The execution proof must run the CLI and observe stdout exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\\n\\\".\",\n          \"Do not write source, tests, package files, or execution plans in this vector.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        stage: \"implementation_design\",\n        filesToProduce: [\"design/implementation-design.md\"],\n        instructions: [\n          \"Write only design/implementation-design.md.\",\n          \"Use the prior conformance_project artifact as authority.\",\n          \"Define a minimal Node CLI script at generated/hello-world.mjs.\",\n          \"The script must print exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\" followed by one newline.\",\n          \"Name component and UAT test source surfaces that execute the CLI and assert stdout.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        stage: \"source\",\n        filesToProduce: [\"generated/hello-world.mjs\"],\n        instructions: [\n          \"Write only generated/hello-world.mjs.\",\n          \"The script must execute under node without package installation.\",\n          \"It must write exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\\n\\\" to stdout.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        stage: \"test_design\",\n        filesToProduce: [\"design/test-design.md\"],\n        instructions: [\n          \"Write only design/test-design.md.\",\n          \"Specify component and UAT validation of the CLI stdout contract.\",\n          \"Both tests must spawn node generated/hello-world.mjs and assert status 0 and stdout exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\\n\\\".\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        stage: \"component_test_source\",\n        filesToProduce: [\"test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs\"],\n        instructions: [\n          \"Write only test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs.\",\n          \"Use node:test, node:assert/strict, and node:child_process spawnSync.\",\n          \"Run process.execPath with [\\\"generated/hello-world.mjs\\\"] from the project root.\",\n          \"Assert status 0 and stdout exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\\n\\\".\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        stage: \"uat_test_source\",\n        filesToProduce: [\"test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs\"],\n        instructions: [\n          \"Write only test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs.\",\n          \"Use node:test, node:assert/strict, and node:child_process spawnSync.\",\n          \"Run process.execPath with [\\\"generated/hello-world.mjs\\\"] from the project root.\",\n          \"Assert the user-visible CLI output is exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\\n\\\".\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        stage: \"test_execution_plan\",\n        workerExecutes: true,\n        filesToProduce: [\"test-execution-plan.json\", \"test-execution-result.json\"],\n        instructions: [\n          \"Write test-execution-plan.json and test-execution-result.json only.\",\n          \"The JSON command must be node.\",\n          \"The args must be [\\\"--test\\\", \\\"test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs\\\", \\\"test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs\\\"].\",\n          \"expectedTestPassCount must be at least 2, matching the admitted component and UAT coverage floor.\",\n          \"expectedStdoutMatch must include stable zero-failure evidence such as fail 0; do not pin an exact pass-count fragment when the generated tests add depth coverage.\",\n          \"assertedReturnValue must be \\\"Hello, world!\\\".\",\n          \"EXECUTION-DEFAULT LAW: run node --test test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs yourself inside this turn; the framework executes nothing.\",\n          \"Record the truthful observed command, args, integer status, stdout, stderr, expectedTestPassCount, expectedStdoutMatch, assertedReturnValue, cwd, and env in test-execution-result.json.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        stage: \"test_execution_result\",\n        instructions: [\n          \"Produce no files.\",\n          \"Accept only if the execution plan command exited 0, observedTestPassCount is at least the prior test_execution_plan expectedTestPassCount, and planSatisfied is true.\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }),\n=== source/witness-contract.md\n# Independent consumer witness\n\nComplete the original basic-cli outcome using the supplied existing candidate,\ndesign, verification artifacts and plan. These files are supplied work, not\nadmitted evidence of success and not the output of a native author in this Run.\nTheir actual behavior has not yet been established in this Run. Evaluate the\ncandidate before deciding what needs changing. Preserve valid work and repair\nonly a materially established implementation defect.\n\nKeep the original source, independent oracle, this contract, design/conformance\ndocuments, test sources and test plan unchanged. Application edits are confined\nto generated/hello-world.mjs. Declared execution evidence may be written under\nexecution-evidence. Other policy/schema assets added by installation are\nprotected. No package installation or network access is needed for this app.\n\nThe complete original source and independent basic-cli oracle govern the\napplication outcome. The added framework discriminator requires an actual\ncommand observation of the supplied candidate, with no native author prerequisite;\nits material failure must remain evidence for a subsequent, different registered\nwork choice. Required independent user-outcome assessment and parent reevaluation\nmust consume current evidence. A child completing an observation does not\ncomplete the application.\n\nThis fixture intentionally supplies an unverified candidate. Do not import\nhistorical successful runtime events or invent author lineage. Do not force an\nexpected graph sequence. An unexpected choice or failure remains the result of\nthe first attempt; preserve it for disposition rather than changing this oracle.\n\n=== specification/project-conformance.md\n# Project conformance\n\nThe application is a minimal Node CLI. Running node generated/hello-world.mjs\nfrom this project emits exactly Hello, world! followed by one newline and exits\nwith status zero. It needs no package installation.\n\nThe original selected source is source/original-basic-cli.txt. Its complete\nbehavior and artifact obligations apply. Its predecessor vector mechanism does\nnot govern this library's execution. This document states the requested outcome;\nit is not a record of successful execution.\n\nImplementation design, test design, component and user-outcome tests, and the\ntest execution plan are retained project assets. Actual execution evidence and\nindependent assessment must establish their satisfaction on the current files.\n\n=== test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs\nimport { test } from 'node:test';\n