{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWNd64YGd86CwPn9WgJn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YKo8FkPtbYy51EH6CJPqqx","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"summary":"I fixed the candidate CLI by adding a missing comma to its output. The only file I changed is generated/hello-world.mjs, where console.log(\"Hello world!\") is now console.log(\"Hello, world!\"). Before the fix, the admitted observations showed the problem: `node generated/hello-world.mjs` exited 0 but printed \"Hello world!\\n\" instead of \"Hello, world!\\n\", and `node --test test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs` exited 1 with pass 0 and fail 2. I confirmed the wrong output locally before editing. After the fix, running `node generated/hello-world.mjs` exits 0 and prints exactly \"Hello, world!\\n\", which is 14 bytes. My first rerun of the test command also exited 0 but ran no tests. My shell had inherited NODE_TEST_CONTEXT=child-v8, so node:test printed \"run() is being called recursively... skipping running files\" and skipped both files. That result is not valid evidence. Rerunning with that variable and NODE_OPTIONS removed (`env -u NODE_TEST_CONTEXT -u NODE_OPTIONS node --test test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs`) exited 0 with tests 2, pass 2 and fail 0. That meets the plan's expectedTestPassCount of 2 and its \"fail 0\" match. I left the original source, oracle, contract, conformance and design documents, test sources and test plan unchanged. These are my own checks; they are not independent acceptance.","gaps":["The only admitted observations predate the fix and show a failure (CLI stdout \"Hello world!\\n\"; tests exited 1, pass 0, fail 2). The passing results after the fix come from my own runs, not from an admitted observation. Fresh runs of the CLI and the plan command on the fixed file are still needed.","The shell inherited NODE_TEST_CONTEXT=child-v8, which makes node --test silently skip the test files and exit 0. Any later execution run should use an environment without it, or a zero-test run could look like a pass.","I did not write test-execution-result.json or anything under execution-evidence. My write access covered only generated/hello-world.mjs, so the truthful execution result required by the test_execution_plan stage is still missing.","The independent user-outcome check, the test_execution_result acceptance decision and the parent reevaluation of support://default-library-witness/complete-source-outcome@5 are all still open."]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":835,"cache_read_input_tokens":25431,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":835},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a323c4a2-7215-4da0-b4c3-f6e9a9a47a57","uuid":"4f79f235-bcf6-4e54-ac26-f1338e85ebbf","timestamp":"2026-09-28T19:16:21.304Z","request_id":"req_011CfWNd5bm7XXCxHws3JWpy","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YKo8FkPtbYy51EH6CJPqqx":{"summary":"I fixed the candidate CLI by adding a missing comma to its output. The only file I changed is generated/hello-world.mjs, where console.log(\"Hello world!\") is now console.log(\"Hello, world!\"). Before the fix, the admitted observations showed the problem: `node generated/hello-world.mjs` exited 0 but printed \"Hello world!\\n\" instead of \"Hello, world!\\n\", and `node --test test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs` exited 1 with pass 0 and fail 2. I confirmed the wrong output locally before editing. After the fix, running `node generated/hello-world.mjs` exits 0 and prints exactly \"Hello, world!\\n\", which is 14 bytes. My first rerun of the test command also exited 0 but ran no tests. My shell had inherited NODE_TEST_CONTEXT=child-v8, so node:test printed \"run() is being called recursively... skipping running files\" and skipped both files. That result is not valid evidence. Rerunning with that variable and NODE_OPTIONS removed (`env -u NODE_TEST_CONTEXT -u NODE_OPTIONS node --test test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs`) exited 0 with tests 2, pass 2 and fail 0. That meets the plan's expectedTestPassCount of 2 and its \"fail 0\" match. I left the original source, oracle, contract, conformance and design documents, test sources and test plan unchanged. These are my own checks; they are not independent acceptance.","gaps":["The only admitted observations predate the fix and show a failure (CLI stdout \"Hello world!\\n\"; tests exited 1, pass 0, fail 2). The passing results after the fix come from my own runs, not from an admitted observation. Fresh runs of the CLI and the plan command on the fixed file are still needed.","The shell inherited NODE_TEST_CONTEXT=child-v8, which makes node --test silently skip the test files and exit 0. Any later execution run should use an environment without it, or a zero-test run could look like a pass.","I did not write test-execution-result.json or anything under execution-evidence. My write access covered only generated/hello-world.mjs, so the truthful execution result required by the test_execution_plan stage is still missing.","The independent user-outcome check, the test_execution_result acceptance decision and the parent reevaluation of support://default-library-witness/complete-source-outcome@5 are all still open."]}}}
